OPAL

Performance-first remote desktop for Linux, Apple Silicon macOS, and Windows.
All platforms use signed rendezvous, end-to-end encrypted direct UDP, blind encrypted relay fallback, and Tailscale when available.

LINUX
=====

Installation

Fedora / Fedora Asahi:

  sudo dnf install -y gcc-c++ make git pkgconf-pkg-config SDL3-devel openssl-devel ffmpeg ffmpeg-devel pipewire pipewire-devel pipewire-pulseaudio libportal libportal-devel xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Arch / CachyOS:

  sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel git pkgconf sdl3 openssl ffmpeg pipewire pipewire-pulse libportal xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Debian / Ubuntu:

  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential git pkg-config libsdl3-dev libssl-dev ffmpeg libavformat-dev libavcodec-dev libavutil-dev libswresample-dev libswscale-dev libpipewire-0.3-dev libportal-dev pipewire pipewire-pulse xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Build and install:

  git clone https://github.com/xt9y/OPAL.git
  cd OPAL
  make -j"$(nproc)"
  sudo make install

Tailscale

  curl -fsSL https://tailscale.com/install.sh | sh
  sudo tailscale up
  tailscale ip -4
  tailscale status

Tailscale is optional. OPAL can still use LAN discovery, signed rendezvous, direct UDP, and relay fallback without it.

Run

  opal
  opal <connection-code>
  opal doctor
  OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal <connection-code>

Choose "Host this computer" on the machine being controlled. On Wayland, select the displays in the xdg-desktop-portal chooser. OPAL can persist and reuse that authorization for later capture sessions.

Backend

  capture      PipeWire + libportal + xdg-desktop-portal, persistent multi-monitor capture
  encode       persistent in-process FFmpeg / hardware H.264 path
  decode       FFmpeg libavcodec
  presentation SDL3
  input        /dev/uinput with multi-monitor absolute pointer mapping
  clipboard    wl-clipboard on Wayland, SDL3 fallback elsewhere
  audio        PipeWire/PulseAudio-compatible capture + SDL3 playback
  service      systemd user service
  network      native UDP with sendmmsg/recvmmsg batching

Optional rendezvous server deployment:

  make rendezvous-server
  make deploy-rendezvous


MACOS
=====

Installation

Requirements: Apple Silicon, macOS 13+, Xcode Command Line Tools, and Homebrew.

  xcode-select --install
  brew install pkg-config sdl3 openssl@3 ffmpeg git
  git clone https://github.com/xt9y/OPAL.git
  cd OPAL
  make
  make install

Do not run sudo make install on macOS. The Makefile builds and signs as the current user and invokes sudo only for the final copies into /usr/local.

Tailscale

Install the Tailscale standalone macOS app, sign in to your tailnet, and enable its CLI integration if you want the tailscale command in Terminal. Then verify:

  tailscale ip -4
  tailscale status

OPAL also detects the CLI bundled inside Tailscale.app. Tailscale is optional; LAN/direct/rendezvous/relay networking remains available without it.

Run

  opal
  opal <connection-code>
  opal doctor
  OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal <connection-code>

For hosting, grant:

  System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Screen & System Audio Recording -> OPAL / opal
  System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Accessibility -> opal-input

The host runs through a per-user launchd LaunchAgent.

Backend

  capture      ScreenCaptureKit with native display timestamps
  encode       hardware VideoToolbox H.264 low-latency encoder
  decode       FFmpeg libavcodec
  presentation SDL3
  input        CGEvent through the Accessibility-authorized opal-input helper
  clipboard    NSPasteboard
  audio        ScreenCaptureKit system audio + persistent AAC + SDL3 playback
  service      per-user launchd LaunchAgent
  network      nonblocking bounded UDP + direct/relay/Tailscale paths


WINDOWS
=======

Installation

Requirements: Windows 10+ and an MSYS2 UCRT64 shell for building OPAL.

In the MSYS2 UCRT64 shell:

  pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-toolchain mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-pkgconf mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-SDL3 mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-openssl mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-ffmpeg make git
  git clone https://github.com/xt9y/OPAL.git
  cd OPAL
  make
  make verify
  make install

The Windows build produces:

  build/opal.exe
  build/opal-input.exe

make install currently leaves the binaries in build/. Keep opal.exe and opal-input.exe together when copying them to another directory.

Tailscale

Install the official Tailscale Windows client and sign in to the same tailnet as the other OPAL computer. The installed Tailscale client includes its CLI; verify with:

  tailscale ip -4
  tailscale status

Tailscale is optional. OPAL can still use LAN discovery, signed rendezvous, direct UDP, and relay fallback without it.

Run

From PowerShell, Command Prompt, or the MSYS2 shell:

  build\opal.exe
  build\opal.exe <connection-code>
  build\opal.exe doctor

The executable is linked as a console application so CLI output remains visible. Hosting persists through an interactive-user Task Scheduler task rather than a Windows service.

Backend

  capture      DXGI Desktop Duplication + D3D11, virtual-desktop multi-monitor composition
  cursor       DXGI pointer metadata + GPU cursor compositor
  encode       D3D11 Video Processor BGRA -> NV12 + Media Foundation hardware H.264 MFT
  decode       FFmpeg D3D11VA with software fallback
  presentation direct D3D11 swapchain + SDL3 CPU fallback
  input        SendInput
  clipboard    CF_UNICODETEXT + event-driven clipboard listener/cache
  audio        WASAPI loopback + persistent AAC + SDL3 playback
  service      interactive-user Task Scheduler task
  network      Winsock2 + LAN/direct/relay/Tailscale paths

Windows multi-monitor capture supports displays on the selected D3D11 adapter. A desktop spanning multiple DXGI adapters is rejected rather than silently dropping displays.
